WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
In 2020, Berlin froze most
rents at their 2019 levels.

2
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.510
For tenants, that sounded
like pure good news.

3
00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.120
Rents were being held down,

4
00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.380
by law. Then reports appeared
of landlords demanding large

5
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.830
payments for furniture before
they would rent a flat out.

6
00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.730
In 2021, Germany's Constitutional
Court struck the law down.

7
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:27.170
So what really happens when a government
makes something cheaper by law?

8
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.760
In this mission, you'll draw a
maximum price on a supply and demand

9
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:33.870
diagram, and see which quantities change.

10
00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:36.300
Then you'll lower the ceiling yourself,

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.200
and work out who gains and who loses.

12
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.120
Your mission: find out what
happens when a government

13
00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.200
makes something cheaper by law.
